From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 08:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] drm/tilcdc: pass no-connector flag for HDMI bridge attach

Pass DRM_BRIDGE_ATTACH_NO_CONNECTOR to drm_bridge_attach() for the
external HDMI bridge so the bridge no longer creates its own connector.
The next change creates a drm_bridge_connector explicitly instead, which
drm_bridge_attach() would otherwise conflict with.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific HDMI bridge attach fix for BeagleBone Black Rev D Qt dashboard]
Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/tilcdc/tilcdc_external.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tilcdc/tilcdc_external.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tilcdc/tilcdc_external.c
index 3b86d002ef62..90aa482cfca9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tilcdc/tilcdc_external.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tilcdc/tilcdc_external.c
@@ -94,7 +94,8 @@ int tilcdc_attach_bridge(struct drm_device *ddev, struct drm_bridge *bridge)
 
 	priv->external_encoder->possible_crtcs = BIT(0);
 
-	ret = drm_bridge_attach(priv->external_encoder, bridge, NULL, 0);
+	ret = drm_bridge_attach(priv->external_encoder, bridge, NULL,
+				DRM_BRIDGE_ATTACH_NO_CONNECTOR);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
